+# Slice 3.C-shell — `yamt --raw` in the shell: the compare window's start and close, the eight commands
+
+Board "Raw compare" row 6 (needs row 4's `yamt-compare`). Product rules: `docs/plan.md` §2 **#93**, **#94**, **#95**,
+**#97** — read them in full. Request: `docs/slices/request-raw-compare.md` rule 1 and "Defaults decided after the
+design". Design: `.omp/run/notes/RawCompareDesign.md` option A §1 (mode), §2 (when the diff runs), §7 (commands,
+`IpcError`). Row 7 (the window's sources) builds on the generated commands and types.
+
+Facts (given):
+
+- `src-tauri/src/args.rs`: `USAGE`, `Invocation::{Merge { repo }, Help, Version}`, `parse` (an unknown argument is a
+  usage error; `--help`/`--version` win). `src-tauri/src/lib.rs:33-54` `run`: `Merge` → `appimage::repo_from_start_dir`
+  (Linux) → `merge(&repo)`; a usage error → `Ending::failure(format!("{problem}\n{USAGE}"))` (exit 2,
+  `outcome.rs:8-35`).
+- `src-tauri/src/window.rs`: `run(session)` → `open_and_wait` (`:41-60`): `with_session(Builder, session)`, settings
+  read once (`start_settings`, `:62-73`), Linux font rendering, `WebviewWindowBuilder` with `background_color` and
+  `initialization_script(start_script(theme))` (`:90-95`, `dataset.theme`), `CloseWatch` (`:98-174`, shared close
+  fallback), after `run_return` the language servers stop and the ending is read. `window_title(root)` (`:97`).
+- `src-tauri/src/commands.rs:11-38` `specta_builder` (one builder for both bins and `export_bindings`), `with_session`
+  (`:40-53`: manages `HostState` and `Mutex<Merge>`, the invoke handler, the page-load hook). Settings commands
+  (`settings.rs`) need only the window's paths, so they work without a merge; the async merge commands hand work to a
+  `spawn_blocking` worker (`merge.rs:150-160` `on_worker`).
+- `src-tauri/src/ipc_error.rs`: `IpcError` (`#[serde(tag = "kind")]`), `From<yamt_session::Error>`,
+  `From<yamt_settings::Error>`. Its TS words: `frontend/src/ui/problemText.ts:100-130` (an exhaustive `switch` on
+  `cause.kind`, so a new kind needs its words in the same commit).
+- Row 4's API (`crates/compare/src/lib.rs`): `TabStore::{open, start, load_tab, set_column, add_tab, close_tab,
+  rename_tab, set_language, show_tab}`, `comparison(&LoadedTab)`, `tab_texts(&LoadedTab)`, the types `TabId`,
+  `Column`, `ColumnVersion`, `ColumnVersions`, `TabLanguage`, `TabEntry`, `TabList`, `CompareStart`, `Comparison`,
+  `TabTexts`, `MAX_COLUMN_BYTES`, `Error::{Locked, Broken, NewerFormat, ReadFailed, WriteFailed, UnknownTab, TooLarge}`.
+- Tauri 2.12 `PathResolver::data_dir()` = the per-user data folder (`~/.local/share` on Linux, `~/Library/Application
+  Support` on macOS, `%APPDATA%` on Windows). The settings folder is `<config_dir>/yamt/` (`crates/settings/src/places.rs:21-27`).
+- Test harness: `src-tauri/src/mock_window.rs` (`open_window*`, `Window::invoke(cmd, args)`, `Window::ending`).
+
+## Target
+
+Owned: `src-tauri/src/{args,lib,window,commands,ipc_error,mock_window}.rs`, `src-tauri/src/compare.rs` (new),
+`src-tauri/AGENTS.md`, `frontend/src/ui/problemText.ts`, `frontend/src/ui/problemText.test.ts`.
+
+Read-only: everything else (`crates/**`, `src-tauri/Cargo.toml`, other `frontend/**`, `frontend/src/ipc/bindings.ts`
+(generated: run `just bindings` locally to typecheck; the orchestrator regenerates it after your patch), `docs/**`,
+`.omp/**`).
+
+Non-goals: the window's sources, stores and views (rows 7–11); a merge window change of any kind; bringing an open
+compare window to the front.
+
+## Contract (fixed; you may add, never change)
+
+```rust
+// args.rs
+pub(crate) enum Invocation { Merge { repo: PathBuf }, Compare, Help, Version }
+// `--raw` → Compare; `--raw` with `--repo` (any order) → Err("--raw compares pasted text and takes no --repo")
+
+// window.rs: the start script always names the window, before the first frame
+//   document.documentElement.dataset.theme = "<dark|light>"; document.documentElement.dataset.window = "<merge|compare>";
+
+// compare.rs — commands (registered in specta_builder; state Mutex<TabStore>, never locked with another Mutex)
+#[tauri::command] #[specta::specta] fn open_compare(..) -> Result<CompareStart, IpcError>;
+#[tauri::command] #[specta::specta] async fn load_tab(.., tab: TabId) -> Result<TabTexts, IpcError>;          // worker; diff outside the lock
+#[tauri::command] #[specta::specta] async fn set_column(.., tab: TabId, column: Column, text: String, version: ColumnVersion) -> Result<Comparison, IpcError>; // worker; diff outside the lock
+#[tauri::command] #[specta::specta] fn add_tab(..) -> Result<TabList, IpcError>;
+#[tauri::command] #[specta::specta] fn close_tab(.., tab: TabId) -> Result<TabList, IpcError>;
+#[tauri::command] #[specta::specta] fn rename_tab(.., tab: TabId, name: String) -> Result<TabList, IpcError>;
+#[tauri::command] #[specta::specta] fn set_tab_language(.., tab: TabId, language: TabLanguage) -> Result<TabList, IpcError>;
+#[tauri::command] #[specta::specta] fn show_tab(.., tab: TabId) -> Result<TabList, IpcError>;
+
+// ipc_error.rs — added kinds
+UnknownTab { tab: TabId },
+ColumnTooLarge { limit: u32 },
+// From<yamt_compare::Error>: ReadFailed/Locked/Broken/NewerFormat → ReadFailed { path, message };
+// WriteFailed → WriteFailed; UnknownTab → UnknownTab; TooLarge → ColumnTooLarge { limit: MAX_COLUMN_BYTES }
+```
+
+## Behaviour
+
+1. **`--help`** prints the new usage: `usage: yamt [--repo <path>]` / `       yamt --raw`, one sentence that `--raw`
+   compares any two pasted texts in two columns, no repository needed, its tabs kept between runs, and a `--raw` line
+   in the option list.
+2. **`Compare`** never opens a `MergeSession`, never runs git, never calls `appimage::repo_from_start_dir`, never
+   manages `Mutex<Merge>` or `HostState`. It builds the app, opens `TabStore` in `<data_dir>/yamt/compare/` and on
+   failure ends before any window with exit 2 and one line: `another yamt --raw window is open (<folder>)` (Locked);
+   `the stored compare tabs <path> cannot be read: <message>; nothing was changed` (Broken, ReadFailed);
+   `the stored compare tabs <path> were written by a newer yamt (format <n>)` (NewerFormat); `no data folder: <error>`.
+   Otherwise it manages `Mutex<TabStore>`, reads the settings and applies the font rendering as the merge window does,
+   opens the window titled `Compare — yamt` with the same size, background and start script (`window = "compare"`),
+   runs `CloseWatch` unchanged, and after `run_return` ends with exit 0 and no message. Split `open_and_wait` so both
+   windows share one builder path (no copied window setup).
+3. **`load_tab`/`set_column`** lock the store only to call it and clone the `LoadedTab`'s handles, then build the reply
+   (`tab_texts`/`comparison`) after the lock is released, on a `spawn_blocking` worker as `merge.rs` does.
+4. **Words** for the two new kinds in `problemText.ts` in the file's style (e.g. "That tab was closed" /
+   "A column holds up to 8 MiB"; the limit from the reply, written as MiB).
+
+## Acceptance
+
+- `args.rs` tests: `--raw` → `Compare`; `--raw --repo p` and `--repo p --raw` → the error; `--raw --help` → `Help`;
+  the usage names `--raw`.
+- `window.rs` test: the start script names the window for both kinds and the theme.
+- `compare.rs` tests through `mock_window` (a window built on a temp data folder): each command's reply for a fresh
+  store (one "Compare 1"); `set_column` then `load_tab` gives the text and differences of `yamt_merge_core::compare`;
+  `UnknownTab` and `ColumnTooLarge` serialise as their kinds; the start-failure words for Locked, Broken, NewerFormat.
+- Real app (`cargo build -p yamt-app`, a fresh `HOME`/`XDG_DATA_HOME`): `target/debug/yamt --raw` from a folder outside
+  any repository opens a window titled "Compare — yamt" (the page is still the merge page until row 11; the title and
+  `document.documentElement.dataset.window === "compare"` are the proof, through the app-session tooling or the
+  devtools console); `<data>/yamt/compare/tabs.json` exists; a second `yamt --raw` exits 2 with the lock line; closing
+  the first exits 0; `yamt --raw --repo x` exits 2 with the usage; in `scripts/conflict-repo.sh /tmp/<dir>`, `yamt --raw`
+  started there leaves `git status --porcelain=v2` and `git ls-files -u` byte-equal before and after.
+- `pnpm -C frontend typecheck` and `test` pass with the regenerated bindings.
+- Commands: `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo test -p yamt-app`,
+  `just arch-check`.
+
+## Skills
+
+`skill://ipc-contract`, `skill://rust-conventions`, `skill://risk-register`, `skill://verification` (plus your
+autoloaded ones). Read `docs/architecture.md` §3.5 and §4 first.
